<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Turing returns eight weeks after starting bupropion XL 150 mg. The nurse telephone check planned for two weeks after the start did not happen: he was abroad at a conference, two calls went unanswered, and no further call was booked. He had a dry mouth and some difficulty falling asleep in the first week, which settled when he took the tablet earlier in the morning, and no headache, tremor, or restlessness. He has missed no doses. His mood is clearly better: he enjoys running again, at about 35 km a week, and has started working on a new problem with real pleasure. He sleeps about seven hours. Libido and erections are back to his usual. He has had fourteen psychotherapy sessions. The breast tissue is smaller and tender only when pressed. He has had no suicidal thoughts. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Missed contact</td><td>Two-week nurse call after starting bupropion not completed</td></tr><tr><td>Bupropion</td><td>Dry mouth and trouble falling asleep in week one, now settled; no missed doses</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual function</td><td>Libido and erections back to his usual</td></tr><tr><td>Running</td><td>About 35 km a week</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9</td><td>7, down from 15</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

